  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Employers pay for people who deliver results and handle people and money. They judge you by outcomes, references and clear stories.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is writing your goal and the evidence employers ask for.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and alternatives to an MBA: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools draft analyses and plans. Routine management reporting shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Judgment, leadership and accountability hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to draft and challenge plans; later, own the people and results.
  </p>

